| A plain object is not a particle — no `_class`, so nothing to dispatch or
| type-test on. Rejected just like a number, and by the same route: the frame
| fails and answers an `Exception`.
|
| Was `fail_handler_return_plain_object.code`.
Ping {} => {
    return { x = 1 }
}

emit Ping {} to this get r
assert r ∈ Exception
assert r.message = "a handler must return a particle — an object with a '_class' field — found an object"
assert 1 = 1
